\title{zurds: Inspect and Safely Read R Serialization Files}
\description{
Reads the files R writes with saveRDS(), save() and serialize(), and lazy-load databases, without handing them to R's deserializer. It reports a file's header, lists the objects in an '.rda' file, summarises the structure of any stream, extracts a single object or list element, and scans for everything that can run code or reach outside the file, such as promises, closures and environments. Data-only files can be read with a reader written in C that builds only vectors, lists and attributes and never evaluates code from the file.
